MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 4775763776648369935}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0882748dc185476197f6ec16b90304dd, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  notesText: 'This object isn''t supposed to be rendered at all!  It''s just a layout
    tool.  We define its height to be 9% of the entire HUD''s height, and position
    it near the top (Anchor Y min is .9, max is .99).


    Then, all children of
    this layout object can have a height 100% of their parent (Anchor Y min 0, max
    1).


    With that strategy, we can resize all of the children by resizing this
    bar.  We can also move all of the children by moving this bar.


    Why is there
    a disabled Image component on this layout object?  That''s there for convenience. 
    You can enable it to see where this object is while editing, and then disable
    it afterwards.

'
